@copilot Update this PR directly to simplify the duplicated suspend-annotation test JVM configuration in instrumentation/kotlinx-coroutines/kotlinx-coroutines-1.0/javaagent/build.gradle.kts. Do not create a follow-up PR.

Remove the nested targets/all/testTask.configure block from the version13Test suite and the separate tasks.test flag-setting block. Replace them with one shared block inside tasks:

```kotlin
withType<Test>().configureEach {
  if (name != "testDisabled") {
    jvmArgs("-Dotel.instrumentation.kotlinx-coroutines-suspend-annotations.enabled=true")
  }
}
```

This follows the existing default-off instrumentation pattern in Hystrix, Hibernate, and Twilio. The ordinary test and version13Test JVMs must still explicitly enable suspend annotations, while testDisabled must leave the property unset and exercise the actual disabled default. Preserve testDisabled's DefaultEnablementTest filter, classpath, testClassesDirs, and check wiring. Keep all test-suite dependencies and the three disabled dispatcher reproductions unchanged. Do not alter production defaults, selector names, emitted scopes, documentation, PR title/description, lower PR #20754, base branch, draft state, or native stack metadata.

Run the narrow module formatter and relevant test, version13Test, and testDisabled tasks using repository conventions. Verify both ordinary suites receive the opt-in and testDisabled receives neither that opt-in nor an explicit false override. Keep the change confined to this Gradle simplification.
